// Walkthrough 1 - the interaction. Level 1: every line given and explained.
// Search-and-measure, because it is the row with no scene setup at all and the
// one the student has already written twice (2.1's trigger, 3.1's range check).
const WALK_INTERACT = {
  ask: 'how do I press E beside a lever and make the lever do something?',
  file: 'Assets/Scripts/PlayerController.cs',
  label: 'In the Code',
  intro:
    'The lever is already wired to the door. What is missing is any way for the player to reach it: press E today and nothing happens, because no line in your controller has ever asked about the E key. The whole interaction is about fifteen lines, and every one is given and explained below.',
  level: 1,
  steps: [
    {
      title: 'Declare how far your reach is',
      lead: 'One field, in the class body, beside `moveSpeed` and the rest: the `[SerializeField] private` pattern from 1.3 — private in code, a knob in the Inspector.',
      lines: [
        {
          code: '    [SerializeField] private float interactRange = 1.5f;',
          what: 'How close counts as **near enough**, in world units. `1.5f` is roughly one player width — a sane first guess for a lever standing on the ground.',
