      lead: 'A brand new file in `Assets/Scripts/`. It has two slots to fill in the Inspector and no other state at all — a listener owns nothing, it only reacts.',
      lines: [
        {
          code: '    [SerializeField] private Lever lever;',
          what: 'A slot holding the lever **component** this door listens to. `Lever` is the type name from `Lever.cs`, so the field can hold nothing else — and an empty slot is a bug you can see before you press Play.',
          why: '**A wired reference rather than a scene search.** You could call `FindFirstObjectByType<Lever>()` in `Start()` here and it would work. The slot is better for this job: a door that listens to a specific lever should say so where a designer can see it. Same argument as the waypoint slots in 4.1 — a reference to a thing **in the scene** belongs to the scene.',
