          what: 'The once-only setup method from 1.3 — the same one that finds your body and seeds your memory in every other script you own. Here it does the subscribing.',
          why: '**Once, and only once.** Put the subscription in `Update()` instead and you add a **new** listener every frame: after one second the lever has sixty subscribers, and one pull calls your method sixty times. It still looks like it works, because switching a door off twice is the same as switching it off once — which is what makes that bug so easy to ship.',
        },
        {
          code: '    {',
          what: '',
        },
        {
          code: '        lever.onLeverOn.AddListener(OpenDoor);',
