          why: '**This is the whole point of the lesson in one line.** The lever stores a reference to your method and calls it later. It does not check what the method does, where it lives, or what the object is for: `OpenDoor` could equally start music or count a coin, and `Lever.cs` would not change by a character. That is what your exam means by abstraction, and it is what the three listeners on `CaveSwitch` are doing already.',
